plugin-hostd-protocol (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * curve_bind and curve_points: a display of an instance's panel
    description bound to the instance's parameters, and drawn from the values
    the instance holds at its rate by omx-dsp's omx_curve_points; codes -536
    to -539.
  * host_dispatch_register_curve(): a host answers both over its backend and
    the rate it gives; one that does not answers -902.
  * Codes -540 (durable-write-failed) and -541 (writer-queue-full) for the
    daemon's writer thread: history_clear, pin_clear and pin_accept declare
    them.
  * curve_points answers -542 (curve-value-not-finite) for a value that is
    not finite; a head filter's slope comes from its enumeration (@12|24).
  * socket_adopt(): a host serves sockets its caller already bound, so a
    supervisor or a harness hands it the port and never closes and binds it
    again; a second bind on the port is refused.
  * Builds with libomxdsp-dev >= 0.32.0 and < 0.33.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 17:22:59 +0100

plugin-hostd-protocol (0.4.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * show_external_ui and hide_external_ui are optional of every profile: the
    daemon sends each to the worker that holds the instance and passes its
    resp back; a daemon with no display session refuses both with -902
    hosting.window.no-display; the ledger keeps the latest of the two.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

plugin-hostd-protocol (0.4.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A second daemon on a busy port is refused instead of silently sharing it:
    the ports are opened with SO_REUSEADDR, never SO_REUSEPORT, so a port the
    daemon before left in TIME_WAIT is still taken again at once.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0100

plugin-hostd-protocol (0.4.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The descriptor name rule says bytes: each byte of an id's UTF-8 text
    outside [A-Za-z0-9._-] is one PHD_DESCRIPTOR_SAFE_CHAR, as plugin-hostd
    reads it and plugin-qualify now writes it.

